# 9. Week 8 Retrospective

## What went well

- Theory-first approach: understanding the IIR resonator structure before coding meant the formula was clear from day 1. The debugging that followed was environmental (trig, namespace), not algorithmic.

- Systematic debugging discipline: the incremental isolation approach (strip to minimum, add one thing at a time) found the root cause after many false hypotheses. Building incrementally rather than guessing was the right call.

- Library audit was thorough and efficient: one grep command identified all trig usage. All four fixed indicators re-validated clean in under an hour.

- Validation metrics appropriate for oscillators: amplitude statistics, zero-mean verification, signal frequency, trend mode comparison, amplitude envelope. These become the oscillator validation template for Weeks 9+.

- Bi-weekly roadmap update (three changes approved) completed before Day 1 theory, keeping program management current.

## What was harder than expected

- The trig bug took significantly longer to diagnose than expected. Multiple false hypotheses (double-call, variable collision, script structure, caching) required before root cause found via alpha_debug diagnostic. Key lesson: compute and output intermediate values before trusting downstream computation.

- The series()-then-overwrite IIR pattern failure was unexpected. Same pattern works in HighPassFilter — understanding why it fails in CyberCycle's specific context required careful analysis of Zorro's flat namespace behavior.

- Test_RoofingFilter.c's "correct-looking" output was based on wrong coefficients — the double-call was masking the trig bug. This means Week 6 validation passed for the wrong reasons. All affected indicators are now properly fixed and re-validated from scratch.

## Heading into Week 9

- Week 9: FRAMA (Fractal Adaptive Moving Average) + Laguerre Filter + Deviation-Scaled MA. Adaptive trend indicators — comparison with MAMA/FAMA drives final Baseline selection for Phase 3.

- The oscillator validation framework (amplitude stats, signal frequency, trend mode comparison, AGC check) is now the template for all future oscillator-type indicators.

- AGC normalization for BTC is a recurring systemic issue. All oscillator-type indicators should check amplitude consistency explicitly — the 10x BTC amplitude variation will appear again.

- The cc_ prefix pattern for Zorro flat namespace is now established. All new indicator files should check for variable name conflicts with existing library files before finalizing.

**Week 8 Complete ✅ — CyberCycle Library Entry Approved (with conditions)**
